fix(agents): correct legacy detection + dispatch slow sweeps in background

- isV2SimulationProfile was returning true for null/undefined profiles
  because getSimulationProfile fills in a default with cohortId set to
  the V2 cohort id. That meant archiveLegacyAgents (and every worker
  that used isV2SimulationProfile to gate v2-only behaviour) treated
  legacy agents as v2 and never archived them. Now check the raw value
  has a record-shaped cohortId match, no defaulting.

- runAgentBatch / runVoteSweep / runCommentSweep can take >30s
  (especially predictions, which call LLMs for world markets). Railway's
  edge gateway 502s after the timeout even though work continues
  server-side. Switch the three admin endpoints to fire-and-forget:
  return immediately with { started: true } and run the sweep in a
  detached promise. Admin UI now shows "started" toasts and refreshes
  status after 5s so the user sees counts climb naturally.
